+# Field notes — righttenantry-security-m1-stripe-payment-status (2026-08-18)
+
+- Squirrel NOT needed here (no schema change): the payment_status enum already
+  had 'pending' as the waiting state; `processed_stripe_event.event_type` is
+  free-form TEXT, so a new arm needs no migration — verify before assuming.
+- Stripe settle choice: `checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded` is
+  session-shaped (reuses complete_payment by session id, zero new SQL);
+  `payment_intent.succeeded` is PI-shaped and CANNOT settle pre-existing
+  rows (stripe_payment_intent_id is only written at completion). Pick the
+  session-shaped event.
+- Event-body fixtures default `payment_status` to "paid" or every
+  pre-existing completed-event integration test silently flips to the
+  fail-closed pending path (consent-capture test bit first).
